cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis, cite it as below."
title: "π🔒 — What a Pi lockup actually is"
abstract: >-
  An independent, source-verified analysis of Pi Network lockups: the official
  lockup reward formula L(B) = Lt * Lp * log(N) * B, the distinction between the
  mining-app lockup setting and the wallet lockup, the on-chain encoding of the
  four lockup durations (exact second counts based on a 365.2425-day Julian year),
  and the PiRC1 section 3 baseline PiPower rule for long-term lockers.
